 ## Background
-The span space concept was introduced by Livnat et al. in the context of the NOISE algorithm [S1]. The technique was developed to address the performance bottlenecks of traditional isosurface extraction methods on large measurement data (such as MRI and CT scans), which often produce large numbers of seed cells and slow preprocessing times [S1]. The method relies on the observation that cells intersecting an isosurface can be identified by a 2D range query on their min/max values.
